# 💭 Reflection - Unit 1: Your First Android App

## 🧠 What I Learned
- ✏️ How to write simple Kotlin programs that display text output
- 🛠️ How to install and configure Android Studio for development
- 🎨 How to build a basic layout with text and images using XML
- ▶️ How to run an app on an emulator or a physical device

## 😅 Challenges
- ⚙️ Setting up Android Studio and the emulator took a lot of patience
- 🧩 XML layouts looked confusing at first, and it took time to understand how they're structured
- 🔗 Linking Kotlin code to UI components needed plenty of practice

## 🤔 My Choices
- 📐 I used a `LinearLayout` because it made arranging text and images simple
- 🖼️ I added a custom image to give the app a personal touch
- 💻 I chose Kotlin because it fits modern Android development practices

## 🏆 Outcome
Finishing Unit 1 gave me real confidence in setting up Android Studio, writing Kotlin code, and designing simple user interfaces. 🎉

This unit built the foundation for my future labs by bringing together language basics and Android SDK principles. On to the next one! 🚀
